  "plain": "In the 1980s a set of papers known as MJ-12 surfaced, said to describe a secret government group handling crashed UFOs, along with a supposed memo briefing President Eisenhower on it, and the researcher who first put them out judged them only \"compelling but not conclusive.\" The writer Greg Bishop tells this, relaying what the researcher Bill Moore said when he released his report on them in a book called The MJ-12 Papers. The point is that even the man who brought the papers to light did not claim they were proven real."
